    "summaryAr": "WHO WE ARE Adikteev is an AdTech company that helps mobile app publishers grow their revenue through targeted advertising. We deliver personalized ads that drive users to install an app or re-engage with one they've stopped using. Our clients are mostly mobile gaming leaders but also span e-commerce, on-demand services, and entertainment apps. Recognized for 10+ years as one of the top mobile retargeting platforms, A",
    "descriptionAr": "WHO WE ARE Adikteev is an AdTech company that helps mobile app publishers grow their revenue through targeted advertising. We deliver personalized ads that drive users to install an app or re-engage with one they've stopped using. Our clients are mostly mobile gaming leaders but also span e-commerce, on-demand services, and entertainment apps. Recognized for 10+ years as one of the top mobile retargeting platforms, Adikteev now operates globally from Paris, San Francisco, Barcelona and Seoul and has grown to over 120 employees. Beyond the business, Adikteev is consistently recognized as a great place to work. With an 18-nationality team, a 4.5-day work week, and a strong focus on inclusion, Adikteev is a place where people genuinely stay. WHAT YOU WILL DO We are looking for a Senior Engineering Team Lead to take ownership of our Reporting platform and lead the team responsible for its evolution. This is a player-coach role for a staff-level data engineer who combines deep technical expertise with strong engineering leadership and people management skills. You will help design, deploy, and evolve the data infrastructure that powers Adikteev’s reporting and analytics systems. You will be both the technical architect of the platform and the manager of the team that enables reliable, scalable, and high-value reporting for our internal and external users. As the team lead, you won't just \"execute\" tasks. You will shape our technical DNA and support the growth of the team. Engineering: Define and drive the technical vision, architecture, and roadmap for our Reporting platform and data infrastructure. Architect, scale, and maintain our data infrastructure, ensuring it meets the rigorous demands of reporting, analytics, and business intelligence workflows. Make sure data is always available and reliable: oversee processing, storage, aggregation, transformation, and API development. Streamline our data processes by integrating efficient testing, monitoring, alerting, incident response, and error recovery. Design and implement robust data models and transformation pipelines that make reporting data easy to discover, understand, and use. Build and optimize highly scalable pipelines using Apache Airflow and Apache Spark, focusing on high reliability, performance, and cost efficiency. Establish best practices for data quality, CI/CD for data, observability, technical documentation, and operational excellence. Contribute to innovation efforts by exploring promising ideas from recent academic and industry work and turning them into production-grade solutions. Leverage AI coding tools such as Copilot and Claude to accelerate development cycles and stay at the forefront of engineering productivity. Remain hands-on where it creates the most leverage, contributing to system design, code reviews, critical implementation work, and incident resolution. Management : Lead, support, and develop the Reporting engineering team, creating the conditions for engineers to do their best work. Set clear objectives, priorities, and expectations for the team, aligned with company and product goals. Manage the team’s roadmap and delivery, balancing business priorities, platform reliability, technical debt, and long-term investments. Provide regular feedback, coaching, and career development support to team members. Mentor Data and Backend Engineers and help them grow their technical scope, ownership, and leadership skills. Participate in recruitment, onboarding, performance reviews, and team planning. Foster a culture of ownership, collaboration, continuous improvement, and high engineering standards. Identify infrastructure bottlenecks and technical risks before they impact the business, and communicate architectural decisions clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders. WHO YOU ARE You might be a great fit for our Reporting team if you have experience in several of the following areas: Experience : Proven track record as a Staff Data Engineer, Lead Data Engineer, Principal Data Engineer, or Engineering Manager with a strong data engineering background. You have worked on production systems where latency, throughput, availability, reliability, and infrastructure cost matter. Data Volume : Experience working with very large-scale data systems. At Adikteev, our platforms process more than 5 billion events per day and reach over 5 million QPS on some services. You are comfortable designing systems that can handle high data volumes, demanding throughput, and strict reliability requirements. Technical Stack : Hands-on expertise with Apache Spark, including tuning and scaling, as well as Apache Airflow and complex DAG orchestration. Kafka streaming, Kubernetes, and AWS are a plus. Coding Skills : You are an \"AI-native\" developer who embraces AI tools to write better and faster code. Hands-on experience with Scala. Python and Java are a plus. Data Modeling : Strong experience designing data models for reporting, analytics, and business intelligence use cases. Experience with dimensional modeling, data warehouses, or data lakes is a plus. Data Transformation : Solid understanding of how to transform raw data into accurate, consistent, and easy-to-use reporting datasets. Experience building or maintaining reporting or analytics platforms is a strong plus. Engineering Leadership : Experience defining technical direction, setting engineering standards, driving execution across teams, and making architectural decisions at staff level. People Management : Experience managing, mentoring, and developing engineers, providing regular feedback, supporting career growth, and building a high-performing team. Communication : Fluent in English and able to articulate complex architectural choices to both technical and non-technical stakeholders. You are comfortable creating alignment across teams and communicating clearly at every level. Please note that, to comply with employment regulations, applicants are required to maintain residen",
