    "summaryAr": "Build new relationships. Win new business. Drive growth. We are looking for an experienced Business Development Manager – New Customer Acquisition to identify and win new customers across Europe. This is a hands-on commercial role for someone who enjoys opening doors, understanding customer challenges and turning opportunities into long-term contractual relationships. You will own the new-business sales process from ",
    "descriptionAr": "Build new relationships. Win new business. Drive growth. We are looking for an experienced Business Development Manager – New Customer Acquisition to identify and win new customers across Europe. This is a hands-on commercial role for someone who enjoys opening doors, understanding customer challenges and turning opportunities into long-term contractual relationships. You will own the new-business sales process from initial prospecting through negotiation and contract signature, working closely with Inside Sales and Customer Success to ensure a smooth transition once the customer comes on board. What you'll do Identify and develop new B2B customer opportunities through targeted prospecting, networking and outreach. Build relationships with high-potential prospects and convert opportunities into new contract and SLA customers. Understand customer needs and create compelling, value-based commercial solutions. Manage the full new-business sales cycle, from discovery and proposal through negotiation and closing. Build clear opportunity and close plans and maintain an accurate, disciplined CRM pipeline. Work within pricing and contract governance requirements while moving opportunities forward effectively. Partner with Inside Sales and Customer Success to ensure a strong handover and onboarding experience. Monitor pipeline, conversion and contract wins to continuously improve sales effectiveness. Bring market, competitor and customer insights back into the business to strengthen our commercial approach. What you bring Ideally 5+ years of B2B sales or business development experience , with a strong track record in new customer acquisition. Experience prospecting for new business and successfully taking opportunities through to close. Strong value-selling, commercial negotiation and closing skills. A structured approach to pipeline and CRM management. Ability to understand customer requirements and translate them into commercially compelling solutions. Persistence and resilience in a target-driven environment. Strong English; additional European languages are an advantage. A degree in Business, Sales, Marketing, Engineering, Supply Chain or a related area is preferred, although relevant professional experience is equally valued. Willingness to travel extensively, typically 3–4 days per week . Find more English Speaking Jobs in France on Arbeitnow",
