    "languages": [],
    "summaryAr": "About the role The Technical Account Manager owns the day-to-day operational relationship with operator and aggregator clients from go-live onward. They give each client a single technical contact who knows their setup, freeing Account Management to focus on commercial growth. They are accountable for the quality of client configurations and for making changes quickly and accurately, within the standards set by Opera",
    "descriptionAr": "About the role The Technical Account Manager owns the day-to-day operational relationship with operator and aggregator clients from go-live onward. They give each client a single technical contact who knows their setup, freeing Account Management to focus on commercial growth. They are accountable for the quality of client configurations and for making changes quickly and accurately, within the standards set by Operations and Compliance, escalating any exceptions. This is not a commercial, first-line support or approval role: the TAM carries no revenue target, handles complex and recurring tickets rather than all of them, and follows published configuration standards rather than setting them. Responsibilities Client ownership after go-live Act as the primary technical and operational contact for newly onboarded clients. Act as the main stakeholder on integration channels after go-live, picking up operational requests and routing anything commercial to the Account Manager. Monitor the period after go-live for latency and early signs of problems that would affect a successful launch, and escalate before the client reports them. Manage key accounts from an operational perspective, supporting clients through changes to their setup. Operational configuration and change Own financial limit changes and RTP updates, applying the current Booming standards and escalating any request that falls outside them. Own tournament configuration where this sits with Customer Success rather than with the Account Manager. Handle general client requests such as media files and thumbnails, which clients may now request directly from the TAM. Handle setup changes: new currencies, new configurations, account migrations and account splits. Issue resolution and escalation Handle daily operational queries and lead the resolution of higher complexity issues across Operations, Platform and SRE. Keep the client informed in plain language during an incident, with content routed through the agreed communication channel. Translate operator needs into clear, prioritised internal requests that an engineer can act on without a second conversation. Process and improvement Monitor internal operational processes: ticket flow, SLAs, escalation paths and release communication. Identify recurring issues and gaps, propose improvements, and implement the ones that are agreed. Keep the client-facing operational documentation current for the accounts in scope. Requirements Experience 3+ years in a technical account management, technical support or operations role in B2B software, ideally iGaming or another integration-heavy environment. Experience owning client relationships after go-live, including incident communication to a demanding counterparty. Experience working to SLAs and defending them internally. Technical Comfortable with APIs, integration patterns and reading logs well enough to triage before escalating. Able to work in a ticketing and documentation stack (Jira, Confluence) and in internal configuration tooling. Able to read and sanity-check configuration data: game options, limits, currencies, jurisdiction settings. SQL or equivalent query ability is an advantage, for checking a claim before raising it. Communication Writes clearly under pressure, in a way that does not create commitments the company has not made. Holds a position with a client when the answer is no, and escalates rather than improvising an exception. Works across Account Management, Operations, Platform and Compliance without owning any of them. Nice to have iGaming operator or aggregator integration experience. Familiarity with regulated market configuration differences across jurisdictions. Experience improving a support or operations process and measuring the result. Good to know What does success in the first 6 months looks like: Named operator accounts have a single technical contact and a documented, current setup. Operational request volume reaching Account Managers drops measurably against the current baseline. Complex issues are resolved inside SLA, with recurring causes identified and at least two fixed at source. Configuration changes are executed without a compliance or limit error. Clients hear about launch-affecting issues from the TAM before they raise them. This full-time position can be a permanent consultant basis for contractors within European Time zone Why Work for Booming Games Founder led. Impact driven. Employee centric. At Booming Games, we're reshaping the iGaming world with our remote-first approach. Our rhythm? Thrilling slot games with captivating features and stunning designs released every two weeks - no exceptions! Here, it's all about co-ownership and real growth. Dive into a diverse team where your input powers every game we craft! Our perks We’re a 100% remote-first company, offering a best-in-class remote experience Competitive package Family-friendly policies Career growth opportunities Zestful working environment Knowledge sharing opportunities Dynamic culture surrounded by industry experts Company social events for team bonding Contact HR Team Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow",
