    "summaryAr": "About the Team The Applied AI Architect team partners with organizations to turn OpenAI's most capable models into meaningful, real-world impact. We work with customers across industries to identify where AI can create value, design secure and scalable solutions, and help those solutions move from early exploration into sustained production adoption. The team brings together technical strategy, customer partnership, ",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team The Applied AI Architect team partners with organizations to turn OpenAI's most capable models into meaningful, real-world impact. We work with customers across industries to identify where AI can create value, design secure and scalable solutions, and help those solutions move from early exploration into sustained production adoption. The team brings together technical strategy, customer partnership, and practical deployment expertise, working closely with Sales, Product, Engineering, Research, and specialist delivery teams. About the Role As Head of Applied AI Architects for Commercial Sales, you will lead OpenAI’s global Applied AI Architect (AAA) organization for Midmarket and SMB. You will lead through frontline managers and own the technical strategy, coverage model, and customer outcomes across both segments, from discovery and evaluation through production adoption and expansion. In Midmarket , you will align AAAs closely with Sales and focus hands-on technical support on opportunities where it can materially improve the outcome. In SMB , you will build a model that reaches more customers through repeatable deployment practices, self-serve technical resources, and partner delivery, with a clear path to specialist support. Location: Austin, TX or San Francisco, CA In this role, you will: Hire, coach, and develop AAA managers across Midmarket and SMB, setting a consistent bar for technical judgment, customer partnership, and execution. Partner with Commercial Sales leadership to prioritize accounts, plan territory coverage, and allocate technical capacity. Set clear criteria for dedicated, pooled, and partner-led support. Set technical standards for how teams qualify use cases, run evaluations, and guide customers into production across ChatGPT, Codex, and the OpenAI API. Set expectations for technical account plans, including milestones for production readiness and adoption. Sponsor critical customer engagements and coordinate with Enablement, Delivery, and partners so customers have a clear owner and next step. Track technical coverage, technical wins, deployment risks, time to production, adoption, and contribution to revenue growth. Use those signals to decide where to invest capacity and which practices to scale. Bring recurring customer needs and deployment blockers to Product and Engineering. You might thrive in this role if you: Have led managers and scaled customer-facing technical teams across multiple regions or customer segments. Have built coverage models that combine hands-on technical engagement with pooled, self-serve, and partner-led support. Build credibility with executives and engineers and coach teams through architecture, security, evaluation, and deployment decisions. Know when to step into a critical technical decision, when to coach through your managers, and when to bring in specialists. Have helped customers move AI or complex software into production and can show measurable gains in adoption or business outcomes. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
