    "summaryAr": "This role is for one of our clients Compensation: $60 - $85 per hour Location: Remote – United Kingdom, Ireland, Germany, Spain, or Switzerland Experience: 7+ Years Employment Type: Full-Time Work Commitment: Approximately 40 Hours per Week Compensation: Based on Location and Experience About the Role We are looking for experienced Senior Marketing Professionals to join the in-house marketing team of a leading AI-foc",
    "descriptionAr": "This role is for one of our clients Compensation: $60 - $85 per hour Location: Remote – United Kingdom, Ireland, Germany, Spain, or Switzerland Experience: 7+ Years Employment Type: Full-Time Work Commitment: Approximately 40 Hours per Week Compensation: Based on Location and Experience About the Role We are looking for experienced Senior Marketing Professionals to join the in-house marketing team of a leading AI-focused organization. This is an opportunity to contribute directly to marketing strategy, execution, and growth initiatives within a technology-driven environment. You will take ownership of a primary marketing discipline aligned with your expertise, such as Product Marketing, Demand Generation, Growth Marketing, Lifecycle Marketing, Brand Marketing, Communications, or Field Marketing. Working closely with cross-functional teams, you will develop and execute marketing programs, support product launches, and drive regional go-to-market initiatives across EMEA. This is a hands-on functional role suited to experienced marketing professionals who can independently lead strategic programs and influence senior stakeholders. Requirements Key Responsibilities Depending on your area of specialization, your responsibilities may include: Developing product positioning, messaging frameworks, value propositions, and launch strategies for products and features. Planning and executing integrated campaigns across demand generation, lifecycle marketing, events, and field marketing. Creating, editing, and reviewing marketing content for technical and business audiences. Monitoring campaign performance and reporting on pipeline contribution, engagement, conversion, and ROI. Collaborating with product, sales, communications, and regional marketing teams to execute go-to-market strategies. Adapting global marketing programs to local markets and regional customer requirements. Using data-driven insights to improve campaign effectiveness and marketing performance. Independently managing strategic marketing initiatives and ensuring successful execution. Core Qualifications 7+ years of professional marketing experience, preferably in in-house roles within technology, AI, or B2B SaaS companies. Strong expertise in at least one of the following marketing disciplines: Product Marketing Demand Generation Growth Marketing Lifecycle Marketing Brand Marketing Marketing Communications Field Marketing Proven experience independently owning and delivering significant marketing programs. Ability to influence senior stakeholders and collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams. Excellent written and verbal communication, content development, and presentation skills. Comfortable working with marketing analytics, performance metrics, and tools such as HubSpot, Salesforce, and Google Analytics. Ability to work in a fast-paced, technology-focused environment. Candidates with exclusively agency-based experience may be less suited to this role. Preferred Candidate Profile Senior marketing professionals with deep expertise in at least one core marketing function. Experienced individual contributors who have independently led strategic initiatives; a formal people-management title is not mandatory. Professionals with backgrounds in AI, technology, enterprise software, or B2B SaaS. Candidates comfortable working with global and regional teams across EMEA. Application Process Submit your updated resume. Complete a short screening questionnaire outlining your experience and marketing specialization. Participate in a short AI-moderated interview. During the interview, select your primary marketing discipline, such as Product Marketing, Demand Generation, or another relevant specialization. Working Language: English for both the role and interview process. Engagement & Compensation Full-time commitment of approximately 40 hours per week. Fully remote opportunity open to candidates based in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Germany, Spain, or Switzerland. The engagement may be structured as an independent contractor arrangement or employment through a local partner, depending on location and applicable requirements. Compensation will be determined based on the candidate's location, experience, and expertise and discussed during the screening process. Find more English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland on Arbeitnow",
