    "languages": [],
    "summaryAr": "About the team The People team helps OpenAI build the teams, capabilities, and working practices needed to deliver on our mission. As AI changes what people and organizations can accomplish, we’re exploring how roles, teams, and ways of working should evolve and putting those ideas into practice within OpenAI. About the role We’re looking for an Organizational Design Lead to help build our organizational design capab",
    "descriptionAr": "About the team The People team helps OpenAI build the teams, capabilities, and working practices needed to deliver on our mission. As AI changes what people and organizations can accomplish, we’re exploring how roles, teams, and ways of working should evolve and putting those ideas into practice within OpenAI. About the role We’re looking for an Organizational Design Lead to help build our organizational design capability and shape how people and AI agents work together. You’ll partner with leaders and People colleagues to understand business goals, examine how work gets done, and design the roles, structures, decision processes, and workflows that help teams succeed. This includes exploring where AI can expand people’s capabilities, how responsibilities should evolve, and where human judgment and accountability are essential. This is a hands-on role. You’ll move between understanding organizational challenges, developing new approaches, testing them with teams, and turning what works into practical tools and methods others can use. You’ll bring a thoughtful perspective on organizations and the ability to make change happen. In this role, you will: Translate business goals into organizational choices. Help leaders identify the work, capabilities, roles, and team structures needed to achieve their goals. Design how people and AI agents work together. Rethink workflows, responsibilities, handoffs, and decision rights as AI capabilities evolve, with clear ownership and human accountability. Improve team effectiveness. Understand where unclear boundaries, coordination costs, or decision processes slow teams down, and develop practical ways to address them. Test ideas in real working environments. Partner with teams to prototype new operating practices, gather feedback, and refine approaches before applying them more broadly. Connect organizational design with technology. Work with People partners, analytics colleagues, and technical teams to turn ideas into useful tools, workflows, and working practices. Build capability across People and leadership. Develop simple frameworks, facilitate working sessions, and help others make sound organizational design decisions. Measure and share what works. Assess changes through business outcomes, quality, speed, team effectiveness, and employee experience, and translate learning into repeatable practices. You might thrive in this role if you: Have meaningful experience in organizational design, operating model development, or organizational effectiveness, with examples of changes you helped implement. Understand organizations as interconnected systems of people, work, technology, incentives, and decisions. Can work credibly with senior leaders while staying close to the practical realities of teams. Bring a design mindset: you listen carefully, make ideas tangible, test assumptions, and adapt based on evidence. Have hands-on experience with AI tools and a thoughtful perspective on how AI could change roles, collaboration, and organizational structures. Combine strategic thinking with execution, moving from an ambiguous question to a useful intervention. Communicate clearly, facilitate difficult conversations, and help people navigate change with empathy and sound judgment. Are curious, collaborative, and willing to revise your approach as technology and organizational needs evolve. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
