    "languages": [],
    "summaryAr": "The role You will run full-cycle GTM hiring across APJ from Singapore, with Japan as a primary market. The hiring is technical and customer-facing: Solutions Architects and Sales Engineers, technical post-sales and support, Enterprise and Commercial sales, and the leaders above them. Most of these people are not applying to job posts, so direct outreach is the core of the job rather than a supplement to it. Business-",
    "descriptionAr": "The role You will run full-cycle GTM hiring across APJ from Singapore, with Japan as a primary market. The hiring is technical and customer-facing: Solutions Architects and Sales Engineers, technical post-sales and support, Enterprise and Commercial sales, and the leaders above them. Most of these people are not applying to job posts, so direct outreach is the core of the job rather than a supplement to it. Business-level Japanese is a requirement. You will screen candidates in Japanese, write outreach in Japanese, and partner with hiring managers and candidates in the Japan market directly. English is the working language of the team. What you will do Run kickoff with each hiring manager and leave it with an agreed bar, scorecard and search strategy, not a list of requirements. Build pipeline yourself. Direct prospecting and referrals should be where most of your hires come from, with agencies as the exception. Screen in Japanese and English, and give hiring managers a clear read on each candidate rather than a summary of their CV. Own process speed. Keep loops tight, chase feedback, and surface where a search is stalling before the hiring manager has to ask. Close. Handle compensation conversations, competing offers and counteroffers, and stay close to candidates through notice periods and relocation. Bring market evidence to leaders: talent availability, compensation gaps, and where a profile or level needs to change for a search to be winnable. Run weekly pipeline reviews with your hiring managers and keep searches moving. Partner with Compensation, People Business Partners and regional leaders to adapt global hiring practice to local market reality. What you bring 7+ years in recruiting, including several years of full-cycle hiring in a high-growth technology company. Time spent in a dedicated sourcing role is an advantage, not a step backwards. Business-level Japanese and professional English. You can screen, write outreach and build trust with senior candidates in both. Based in Singapore, with working knowledge of APJ talent markets beyond Japan. A track record hiring technical customer-facing talent: Sales Engineering, Solutions Architecture, technical post-sales or support engineering, plus Enterprise sales and leadership hires. Evidence that you source. You can talk about where your hires actually came from and what your direct-prospecting share looked like. Comfort using compensation and pipeline data to change a leader's mind about a profile, a level or a band. Credibility with senior stakeholders, including the ability to disagree with a hiring manager and hold a bar. Comfort in a fast-moving, open-source-rooted company where process is something you help build rather than inherit. Nice to have Experience hiring in Korea, India or ASEAN alongside Japan. Having built a function or a market from the first hire rather than joining an established one. Experience with databases, observability, developer tools or open-source infrastructure. Mentoring or onboarding other recruiters. Working knowledge of Ashby or a comparable modern ATS. Perks Flexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries. Healthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare. Equity in the company - Every new eligible team member who joins our company receives equity. Time off - Flexible time off in the US, generous entitlement in other countries. A USD$500 Home office setup if you’re a remote employee. Global Gatherings – We believe in the power of in-person connection and offer opportunities to engage with colleagues at company-wide offsites. Culture - We All Shape It As part of a rapidly scaling start-up, you will be instrumental in shaping our culture. Are you interested in finding out more about our culture? Learn more about our values here . Check out our blog posts or follow us on LinkedIn to find out more about what’s happening at ClickHouse. Equal Opportunity & Privacy ClickHouse provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type based on factors such as race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Please see here for our Privacy Statement.",
