    "summaryAr": "The Role We’re hiring a Regional Vice President to lead and scale our Spanish-speaking Latin America business. You’ll own the regional sales strategy and execution, building and leading a high-performing team of Enterprise AEs and turning a growing base of developer adoption and ClickHouse Cloud sign-ups into a durable enterprise business. You’ll be responsible for driving growth across key Spanish-speaking LATAM mar",
    "descriptionAr": "The Role We’re hiring a Regional Vice President to lead and scale our Spanish-speaking Latin America business. You’ll own the regional sales strategy and execution, building and leading a high-performing team of Enterprise AEs and turning a growing base of developer adoption and ClickHouse Cloud sign-ups into a durable enterprise business. You’ll be responsible for driving growth across key Spanish-speaking LATAM markets, developing strategic customer relationships, and establishing ClickHouse as a leading platform for real-time analytics and data infrastructure across the region. You’ll partner closely with our existing Brazil leadership and broader global GTM organization to accelerate growth and build a strong, consistent operating culture. If you’ve successfully built and scaled enterprise sales teams in Latin America and want to do it again with a technically differentiated product, this role is for you. What You’ll Do Own the regional strategy. Develop and execute the go-to-market strategy for Spanish-speaking LATAM, determining which countries, industries, and accounts to prioritize and where to invest in sales coverage. Build and scale the team. Recruit, develop, and lead a high-performing team of Enterprise AEs across the region. Leverage your network to attract top talent and establish a culture of accountability, collaboration, and strong execution. Own the number. Carry the regional quota and deliver accurate weekly, monthly, and quarterly forecasts. Establish rigorous pipeline management, deal reviews, and qualification standards using MEDDPICC or a similar methodology. Land and expand enterprise accounts. Convert existing ClickHouse Cloud and open-source usage into committed enterprise agreements, then expand those relationships as new use cases emerge. Build relationships with strategic enterprise customers across key LATAM markets and industries. Lead strategic deals. Engage directly in executive meetings, strategic opportunities, and complex negotiations. Help your team navigate multi-stakeholder sales cycles involving technical buyers, procurement, legal, and security teams. Build strong cross-functional partnerships. Work closely with Solutions Architects and Sales Engineers to ensure opportunities are technically sound and customers are positioned for long-term success. Drive the full GTM motion. Partner with Marketing, Partners/Alliances, cloud providers, and our product-led growth organization to generate pipeline, develop strategic partnerships, and convert self-service customers into enterprise opportunities. Develop the regional ecosystem. Establish ClickHouse’s presence across Spanish-speaking LATAM by building executive relationships with customers, partners, and the broader data and developer community. Represent ClickHouse at regional events, meetups, and industry programs. Collaborate across LATAM and globally. Partner with Brazil leadership and global GTM teams to share best practices, align on regional priorities, and ensure a consistent approach to building and growing the business. What You Bring 10+ years of enterprise software sales experience in data infrastructure, databases, analytics, observability, or cloud, including a strong record as a quota-carrying seller. 5+ years of experience leading enterprise sales teams, ideally as a first- or second-line leader, with a consistent track record of quota attainment. Proven experience building and scaling enterprise sales teams or territories across Latin America, ideally in a high-growth technology environment. Deep understanding of the Spanish-speaking LATAM enterprise market, including regional business practices, buying behaviors, and the ability to navigate different markets and cultures. An established network of enterprise customers, sales talent, and strategic partners across Spanish-speaking Latin America. Fluency in Spanish and English, with the ability to lead customer, executive, and internal conversations in both languages. Strong forecasting, pipeline management, and qualification discipline (MEDDPICC or similar). You know the difference between a commit and a hope, and your leadership can trust your call. Technical fluency. You can engage in architecture conversations with data engineers and CTOs and understand how to position technical products in complex enterprise environments. Experience with consumption-based or usage-based pricing models and an understanding that in a consumption business, the signed deal is where the revenue starts. A builder mentality. You’re comfortable operating in a growing organization, creating structure where needed, and balancing strategic leadership with hands-on involvement in deals. The ClickHouse DNA: integrity, hunger, and accountability. You’re curious, serious about the craft, and happy to roll up your sleeves. Nice to Have Experience as an early sales leader or founding regional leader at a high-growth data or infrastructure company. Background selling open-source or developer-led products alongside a product-led growth funnel. Familiarity with real-time analytics, OLAP and columnar databases, observability, or AI/LLM workloads. Established relationships with data and technology leaders at major enterprises across Mexico, Colombia, Argentina, Chile, and other Spanish-speaking LATAM markets. Experience building and managing geographically distributed teams across multiple Latin American countries. Experience co-selling with AWS, GCP, or Azure and transacting through cloud marketplaces. Perks Flexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries. Healthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare. Equity in the company - Every new eligible team member who joins our company receives equity. Time off - Flexible time off in the US, generous entitlement in other countries. A USD$500 Home office setup if you’re a remote employee. Global Gatherings – We believe in the po",
