    "summaryAr": "The Role We're hiring a Country Manager to lead and grow our Brazil business. You'll own the country sales strategy and execution, building and developing a high-performing enterprise sales team and turning a growing base of developer adoption and ClickHouse Cloud sign-ups into a durable enterprise business. As the senior sales leader for Brazil, you'll drive regional revenue growth, develop strategic customer relati",
    "descriptionAr": "The Role We're hiring a Country Manager to lead and grow our Brazil business. You'll own the country sales strategy and execution, building and developing a high-performing enterprise sales team and turning a growing base of developer adoption and ClickHouse Cloud sign-ups into a durable enterprise business. As the senior sales leader for Brazil, you'll drive regional revenue growth, develop strategic customer relationships, and establish ClickHouse as a leading platform for real-time analytics and data infrastructure in the market. You'll work closely with our Area VP, Latin America, to align on regional strategy, share best practices, and accelerate growth across the broader LATAM business. This is an opportunity for a hands-on sales leader who understands the Brazilian enterprise technology market, has a strong track record of building teams and delivering results, and wants to help scale a high-growth technology business. This role reports to the Area Vice President, Latin America. What You'll Do Own the Brazil business. Develop and execute the country go-to-market strategy, determining which accounts, industries, and opportunities to prioritize to drive sustainable growth. Build and develop the team. Recruit, lead, and develop a high-performing team of Enterprise AEs. Establish clear expectations, coach performance, and build a culture of accountability and execution. Own the number. Carry the country quota and deliver accurate weekly, monthly, and quarterly forecasts. Establish rigorous pipeline management, deal reviews, and qualification standards using MEDDPICC or a similar methodology. Land and expand enterprise accounts. Convert existing ClickHouse Cloud and open-source usage into committed enterprise agreements, then expand those relationships as new use cases emerge. Develop strategic customer relationships across Brazil's largest enterprise accounts. Lead strategic deals. Engage directly in executive meetings, strategic opportunities, and complex negotiations. Help your team navigate multi-stakeholder sales cycles involving technical buyers, procurement, legal, and security teams. Build strong cross-functional partnerships. Work closely with Solutions Architects and Sales Engineers to ensure opportunities are technically sound and customers are positioned for long-term success. Drive the full GTM motion. Partner with Marketing, Partners/Alliances, cloud providers, and our product-led growth organization to generate pipeline, develop strategic partnerships, and convert self-service customers into enterprise opportunities. Develop the local ecosystem. Establish ClickHouse's presence in Brazil by building relationships with customers, partners, and the broader data and developer community. Represent ClickHouse at executive events, meetups, and industry programs. Collaborate across LATAM and globally. Partner with the Area VP, Latin America, and other regional leaders to align on priorities, share best practices, and ensure a consistent approach to building and growing the business. What You Bring 10+ years of enterprise software sales experience in data infrastructure, databases, analytics, observability, or cloud, including a strong record as a quota-carrying seller. 5+ years of experience leading enterprise sales teams, ideally as a first- or second-line leader, with a consistent track record of quota attainment. Proven experience building and scaling enterprise sales teams or territories in Brazil, ideally within a high-growth technology environment. Deep understanding of the Brazilian enterprise technology market, including local business practices, buying behaviors, and complex enterprise sales cycles. An established network of enterprise customers, sales talent, and strategic partners across Brazil. Fluency in Portuguese and English, with the ability to lead customer, executive, and internal conversations in both languages. Strong forecasting, pipeline management, and qualification discipline (MEDDPICC or similar). You know the difference between a commit and a hope, and your leadership can trust your call. Technical fluency. You can engage in architecture conversations with data engineers and CTOs and understand how to position technical products in complex enterprise environments. Experience with consumption-based or usage-based pricing models and an understanding that in a consumption business, the signed deal is where the revenue starts. A builder mentality. You're comfortable operating in a growing organization, creating structure where needed, and balancing strategic leadership with hands-on involvement in deals. The ClickHouse DNA: integrity, hunger, and accountability. You're curious, serious about the craft, and happy to roll up your sleeves. Nice to Have Experience as an early sales leader or founding country leader at a high-growth data or infrastructure company. Background selling open-source or developer-led products alongside a product-led growth funnel. Familiarity with real-time analytics, OLAP and columnar databases, observability, or AI/LLM workloads. Established relationships with data and technology leaders at major Brazilian enterprises. Experience co-selling with AWS, GCP, or Azure and transacting through cloud marketplaces. Perks Flexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries. Healthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare. Equity in the company - Every new eligible team member who joins our company receives equity. Time off - Flexible time off in the US, generous entitlement in other countries. A USD$500 Home office setup if you’re a remote employee. Global Gatherings – We believe in the power of in-person connection and offer opportunities to engage with colleagues at company-wide offsites. Culture - We All Shape It As part of a rapidly scaling start-up, you will be instrumental in shaping our culture. Are you interested in finding out more about ",
