    "summaryAr": "About the Team The Hardware Marketing team helps people understand what OpenAI’s hardware products can do and how they can fit into everyday life. We work with Product Marketing, Design, Creative, Sales, and Operations to bring new products to market and create experiences that let people experience the magic of the products themselves. About the Role We’re looking for a Channel Lead to build OpenAI’s retail experien",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team The Hardware Marketing team helps people understand what OpenAI’s hardware products can do and how they can fit into everyday life. We work with Product Marketing, Design, Creative, Sales, and Operations to bring new products to market and create experiences that let people experience the magic of the products themselves. About the Role We’re looking for a Channel Lead to build OpenAI’s retail experience and channel marketing programs for consumer hardware. You’ll set the standard for how customers discover, try, and learn about our products. The role calls for creative judgment and hands-on operating experience: you should be as comfortable reviewing a demo on a store floor as you are deciding where to invest next. You’ll own the customer-facing experience and channel marketing strategy, working with Sales and Sales Operations, which own commercial terms, revenue targets, forecasting, and inventory. In this role, you will: Set the retail strategy. Define what our own experiences and third-party retail each do for customers. Decide what to pilot, where to invest, and what to scale based on what we learn. Build OpenAI-owned experiences. Lead the customer journey from first impression and hands-on demo through purchase and support. Work with Design, Creative, production partners, and Operations on spaces, programming, staffing, and day-to-day execution. Lead channel marketing with retail partners. Build joint launch and marketing plans with retailers. Set the standard for fixtures, displays, signage, demos, and online product pages, and give partner teams the tools to execute consistently across stores and markets. Get stores ready for launch. Work with Engineering, IT, Commerce, and Operations to make demos reliable and resolve issues before and after launch. Build the capability from the ground up. Set priorities and budgets, lead cross-functional teams and agencies, and turn what works into playbooks other teams and markets can use. Measure what customers learn and do. Use customer feedback, field observations, engagement, and conversion to improve the experience. Work with Analytics and Sales to understand sales impact and decide which programs to expand. You might thrive in this role if you have: Led consumer retail experience or channel marketing programs across both brand-owned environments and major third-party retailers. Brought consumer technology products to market and made unfamiliar capabilities easy to understand through hands-on demos, merchandising, and clear product storytelling. Built programs that hold up in the field, from associate training and demo readiness to consistent execution across stores or markets. Managed budgets and agency partners, and led creative, technical, operational, and commercial teams through complex launches. Used customer insight and performance data to make decisions about what to improve, stop, or scale. Built a new function or program and enjoy moving between setting the strategy and solving problems on the ground. Experience introducing a new product category or adapting a retail program across markets is a plus. Workplace & Location This role is based in San Francisco, CA. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
