    "summaryAr": "About the Team The Hardware Marketing team helps people understand what OpenAI’s hardware products can do and how they can fit into everyday life. We work with Product Marketing, Design, Creative, Sales, and Operations to bring products to market and create experiences where people can try them for themselves. About the Role We’re looking for a Visual Merchant to shape how customers discover, understand, and try Open",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team The Hardware Marketing team helps people understand what OpenAI’s hardware products can do and how they can fit into everyday life. We work with Product Marketing, Design, Creative, Sales, and Operations to bring products to market and create experiences where people can try them for themselves. About the Role We’re looking for a Visual Merchant to shape how customers discover, understand, and try OpenAI hardware in stores. Reporting to the Channel Lead, you’ll own visual merchandising for OpenAI-owned experiences and third-party retail. You’ll work with Creative, Design, and retail partners to build displays that tell a clear product story and make it easy for customers to get hands-on. You’ll take the work from concept through installation, setting a standard in our own spaces and adapting it for partner stores. You’ll be as comfortable giving feedback on a prototype as you are walking a store to see what customers notice, touch, and miss. In this role, you will: Make the product story visible. Set the order in which customers see products, signage, and demos. Work with Product Marketing and Creative to keep claims accurate and give customers a clear place to start. Develop visual merchandising for OpenAI experiences. Work with Design, Creative, and production partners on fixture placement, displays, signage, and hands-on demo stations. Use mockups and site visits to check sightlines, accessibility, and flow. Develop the experience for global retail partners. Define what needs to stay consistent across stores and what can change for different footprints, retailer standards, and local markets. Review partner concepts, samples, and layouts before rollout. Turn standards into tools store teams can use. Create layout guides, fixture and signage specifications, and setup and reset instructions. Partner with Production and Retail Operations on prototypes, installation, and quality checks so displays are safe and can be maintained day to day. Use what you see in stores to improve the work. Watch how customers approach and use displays, gather feedback from store teams, and check whether installations match the brief. Use what you learn to fix issues and update the next rollout. You might thrive in this role if you have: Built visual merchandising for physical retail and can show how you took work from concept through installation. Experience with both brand-owned and partner stores is a plus. Made a complex product easy to discover and try through strong spatial layout, signage, and demo presentation. Experience with consumer technology or hands-on product demos is a plus. Translated creative direction into practical layouts, specifications, and guides that store teams and vendors can use. Worked with Creative, Design, Production, Operations, and retail partners to solve on-site issues and maintain a consistent standard across locations. Used store observations or customer feedback to improve what people notice and understand, and know how to keep displays accessible and maintainable. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
