    "languages": [],
    "summaryAr": "Developers decide what’s interesting long before they decide what to buy. They follow builders, share the talk everyone is watching, and argue about benchmarks in the replies. Most infrastructure brands show up in that feed looking and sounding the same. ClickHouse has the material to do something different: a fast, open-source database that has grown into a platform for real-time analytics, data warehousing, observa",
    "descriptionAr": "Developers decide what’s interesting long before they decide what to buy. They follow builders, share the talk everyone is watching, and argue about benchmarks in the replies. Most infrastructure brands show up in that feed looking and sounding the same. ClickHouse has the material to do something different: a fast, open-source database that has grown into a platform for real-time analytics, data warehousing, observability, and AI workloads; engineers and leaders with real points of view; and a brand that already turns up in unexpected places, from a Premier League partnership to our own Open House conference. We are looking for a Senior Social Media Manager to run the ClickHouse accounts and turn that material into a brand developers actually want to follow, at the intersection of infrastructure, technology, and culture. You’ll own our presence on LinkedIn, X, and YouTube with video at the center: clipping talks, podcasts, launches, and live moments into content that travels, building formats people come back for, and working with the creators developers already trust. You’ll be accountable for growing audience and engagement across a global community. You’ll sit on the Story & Communications team, reporting to the Head of Story & Communications, and work closely with developer relations, product marketing, demand generation, events, and our brand and design team. This is a hands-on role: you’ll make the work, not only schedule it. What You Will Be Doing Run the ClickHouse accounts on LinkedIn, X, and YouTube end to end: strategy, voice, calendar, publishing, and community management, with an approach built for each channel and for a global audience across time zones Put video at the center of how ClickHouse shows up: clip talks, podcasts, livestreams, launches, and executive moments into short-form and vertical content, and build recurring, social-first series that earn a following Build a brand developers find interesting at the intersection of infrastructure, technology, and culture, pairing technical depth with humor, opinion, and craft Work with the creators and technical voices developers already follow, through collaborations, co-created content, guest appearances, and amplification, in tandem with developer relations and the wider marketing team Turn launches, announcements, customer stories, and research into social moments, and bring live coverage from Open House and industry events, working with regional teams so local moments reach a global audience Grow the voices around the brand: partner with communications on executive presence on LinkedIn and X, and give employees and developer advocates what they need to share their work Own the numbers for organic social, including audience growth, engagement, video performance, and share of the developer conversation, and report on what’s working and why Track what developers say about ClickHouse and the category and feed it back to product marketing, developer relations, and campaign teams, while using AI tooling and a lean production workflow to ship content quickly and partnering with demand generation so the best organic work gets paid reach What You Bring Along A record of growing audience and engagement at scale for a brand with a global following, and the numbers to show it Real fluency with video: you can shoot, edit, and clip yourself, you know what makes short-form and vertical content work on each platform, and you can find the best ninety seconds in an hour-long talk Experience running influencer or creator programs: finding the right voices, structuring partnerships, and making the collaboration feel native to the creator’s audience Experience with a technical or B2B audience, and the ability to turn technical substance into something people want to share Preferred: experience in SaaS, developer tools, or infrastructure Taste and a point of view on internet culture: you know where developers spend time online, what they find funny, and what makes them tune a brand out Sharp short-form writing: the post, the hook, the caption, the thread A builder’s approach: you test quickly, read the data honestly, scale what works, and drop what doesn’t Comfort owning a channel end to end while working across many teams, with low ego and high standards Perks Flexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries. Healthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare. Equity in the company - Every new eligible team member who joins our company receives equity. Time off - Flexible time off in the US, generous entitlement in other countries. A USD$500 Home office setup if you’re a remote employee. Global Gatherings – We believe in the power of in-person connection and offer opportunities to engage with colleagues at company-wide offsites. Culture - We All Shape It As part of a rapidly scaling start-up, you will be instrumental in shaping our culture. Are you interested in finding out more about our culture? Learn more about our values here . Check out our blog posts or follow us on LinkedIn to find out more about what’s happening at ClickHouse. Equal Opportunity & Privacy ClickHouse provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type based on factors such as race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Please see here for our Privacy Statement.",
