    "summaryAr": "About the Team The Global Events & Experiences team brings customers, developers, and other communities together to experience OpenAI’s technology firsthand. Our portfolio spans flagship events, developer programs, and executive gatherings that help people understand what they can do with our products. About the Role We’re looking for a Global Events Strategy & Operations Lead to serve as a strategic and operational ",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team The Global Events & Experiences team brings customers, developers, and other communities together to experience OpenAI’s technology firsthand. Our portfolio spans flagship events, developer programs, and executive gatherings that help people understand what they can do with our products. About the Role We’re looking for a Global Events Strategy & Operations Lead to serve as a strategic and operational partner to the Global Head of Events. You’ll turn OpenAI’s event strategy into a global portfolio plan, helping the team decide where to invest, how to allocate resources, and how to measure the impact of its work. You’ll also lead priority initiatives across the team and own critical workstreams for flagship events and executive experiences, from early scoping through onsite delivery. In this role, you will: Lead portfolio planning. Partner with the Global Head of Events on annual and quarterly planning. Forecast spend and team capacity, surface trade-offs, and recommend which events to invest in, sequence, or defer. Build how the team operates. Develop clear processes and reusable playbooks for evaluating requests, approving investments, and delivering events globally. Use AI and automation to reduce manual work. Drive strategic initiatives. Lead priority projects on behalf of the Global Head of Events. Bring the right partners together, clarify who owns each decision, and resolve dependencies that could delay delivery. Deliver flagship events. Own critical workstreams for flagship events and executive experiences, from defining scope and negotiating with agencies through onsite execution. Partner closely with event leads and creative and technical production teams. Lead performance and business reviews. Give leadership a clear view of spend, outcomes, and decisions that need attention. Use audience feedback and post-event results to recommend changes for the next planning cycle. You might thrive in this role if you have: 8+ years of experience in event strategy, event operations, experiential marketing, or related roles, with experience delivering complex live events. Experience planning across a portfolio of programs, forecasting budgets and capacity, and making recommendations when priorities compete. A track record of building processes and tools that help cross-functional teams make decisions and deliver work consistently. Hands-on experience scoping event work, negotiating with agencies or vendors, and making sound decisions onsite as plans change. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to turn budget, performance, and audience data into clear recommendations for senior leaders. Workplace and Location This role is based hybrid in San Francisco. Occasional travel will be required. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
