    "summaryAr": "About the Role: ClickHouse is looking for a Sr. Account Executive to help expand our presence within large government agencies and the GovCon ecosystem. In this role, you’ll own the full sales cycle with federal customers—from building Pipeline through closing complex deals. Successful candidates are disciplined in their sales process, strong at developing pipeline, and comfortable navigating complex federal buying e",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Role: ClickHouse is looking for a Sr. Account Executive to help expand our presence within large government agencies and the GovCon ecosystem. In this role, you’ll own the full sales cycle with federal customers—from building Pipeline through closing complex deals. Successful candidates are disciplined in their sales process, strong at developing pipeline, and comfortable navigating complex federal buying environments. You’ll work closely with sales leadership, sales engineering, marketing, developer relations, and customer success to help organizations adopt ClickHouse’s Government offerings. What You Will Be Doing: Own the full sales cycle from prospecting through close Build and manage pipeline within a defined set of Public Sector Accounts Lead discovery, qualification, and deal strategy using frameworks such as MEDDPICC Communicate value to technical stakeholders, executive leaders, and buyers Understand and articulate technical differentiation — including performance benchmarks, architecture, and deployment models — at a level of depth that earns credibility with data engineers, architects, PMs and Technical Leads Partner with Sales Engineering, Public Sector Partner Team, and Customer Engineering to support evaluations and technical validation Manage complex Federal sales cycles including procurement, legal, security reviews, and multi-product negotiations Maintain accurate pipeline visibility and forecasting Consistently meet or exceed revenue and pipeline targets Travel to customer sites, conferences, and team offsites as needed (approximately 25%) What You Bring: 8+ years selling Enterprise Data Platforms into federal organizations and projects Demonstrated track record closing large, complex deals ($500K+ ACV) with long sales cycles involving multiple stakeholders Deep understanding and experience selling as a trusted advisor to federal stakeholders Excellent communication, relationship-building, and negotiation skills Comfortable operating in fast-growing environments with evolving processes Desired Qualifications: Prior experience selling open-source or consumption-based products Experience with real-time analytics, time-series databases, OLAP, columnar data systems, or DBMS Startup experience a plus Perks Flexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries. Healthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare. Equity in the company - Every new eligible team member who joins our company receives equity. Time off - Flexible time off in the US, generous entitlement in other countries. A USD$500 Home office setup if you’re a remote employee. Global Gatherings – We believe in the power of in-person connection and offer opportunities to engage with colleagues at company-wide offsites. Culture - We All Shape It As part of a rapidly scaling start-up, you will be instrumental in shaping our culture. Are you interested in finding out more about our culture? Learn more about our values here . Check out our blog posts or follow us on LinkedIn to find out more about what’s happening at ClickHouse. Equal Opportunity & Privacy ClickHouse provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type based on factors such as race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Please see here for our Privacy Statement.",
