    "summaryAr": "About Ramp Ramp is building the smart infrastructure for finance teams, embedded in the transaction flow of every dollar a business spends. We automate how over $275B in annualized spend flows in and out of 85,000+ companies: authorizing payments, flagging risk, categorizing spend, and closing books. The problems are high-stakes, data-dense, and unforgiving. We hire people with high agency and high urgency. We look f",
    "descriptionAr": "About Ramp Ramp is building the smart infrastructure for finance teams, embedded in the transaction flow of every dollar a business spends. We automate how over $275B in annualized spend flows in and out of 85,000+ companies: authorizing payments, flagging risk, categorizing spend, and closing books. The problems are high-stakes, data-dense, and unforgiving. We hire people with high agency and high urgency. We look for slope over intercept. We care less about where you trained and more about what you’ve built. At Ramp, everyone is a builder who owns problems end to end and makes consequential decisions that shape the outcome. The median Ramp customer saves 7.5% and grows revenue 16% in their first year – far in excess of businesses operating without Ramp. We believe every ambitious company deserves the same. If you want to build systems that directly shape how companies move and manage billions, Ramp is the place to do it. About the Role Ramp’s Franchise Channel is growing rapidly, and we’re looking for a self-motivated Partner Development Representative to help build the top of the funnel. As an early member of the team, you’ll identify and qualify new franchise partnership opportunities and help shape the outreach and sourcing strategy for a growing channel. You’ll be the first point of contact for prospective partners, building relationships with franchisor leaders and introducing them to the value Ramp can bring to their businesses and franchise networks. You’ll work closely with Channel Partner Managers to create qualified opportunities that can grow into successful, long-term partnerships. What You’ll Do Identify and source new franchise partnership opportunities through inbound qualification, research, and outbound outreach. Engage and qualify prospective partners through calls, emails, social channels, conferences, and events. Research franchise brands and organizations to understand their business models, franchise networks, key stakeholders, and potential fit for Ramp. Build relationships with decision-makers and stakeholders across franchise organizations, including franchisors and franchisees where relevant. Educate prospective partners on Ramp and its partnership program, connecting Ramp’s value to their business and franchise network. Conduct discovery to understand a prospect’s priorities, challenges, and interest in partnering with Ramp. Set qualified meetings and collaborate with Channel Partner Managers on thoughtful handoffs and next steps. Partner with Marketing, Operations, and Direct Sales to generate opportunities and grow Ramp’s franchise partner ecosystem. Experiment with new sourcing and outreach strategies, sharing feedback and helping build and improve the channel’s workflows and sales motion. Maintain accurate partner relationship and activity data in Salesforce. What You Need Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build trust with a range of stakeholders. Excellent listening skills and an energetic, professional phone and Zoom presence. Comfort with prospecting, outbound sales, and engaging prospects virtually and in person. Curiosity and a desire to understand the challenges facing franchise businesses and their networks. A commitment to tracking and improving your performance and efficiency on a daily basis. An entrepreneurial mindset: you’re a self-starter with a high sense of urgency who can navigate undefined processes and find a way forward. A collaborative approach and enthusiasm for building something new as part of a growing team. Nice to Haves Background in a client-facing or sales role, such as business development or partnerships. Experience selling to or working with franchisors, franchisees, or multi-location businesses. Prior CRM experience, preferably Salesforce. Experience at a high-growth startup. Interest in financial services and how businesses manage their finances. Bachelor’s degree from a four-year university. Benefits available to all full-time Ramp employees (Global) Flexible PTO Centralized home-office equipment ordering Health and wellness stipend Budget for intra-office travel Weekly coffee stipend United States 100% medical, dental & vision insurance coverage for you, with partial coverage for dependents One Medical annual membership 401(k), including employer match on contributions made while employed by Ramp Fertility HRA (up to $10,000 per year) Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay Pet insurance In-office perks: lunch, snacks, drinks, and more Relocation expense coverage to NYC or SF (if needed) Canada Group medical, dental, and vision coverage through Sun Life Life, AD&D, and disability coverage Fertility drug coverage (up to $4,000 lifetime) Group Retirement Plan with employer match (RRSP + DPSP) Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay, with additional time available at reduced pay Employee Assistance Program and virtual care through Lumino Health United Kingdom Private medical insurance through Freedom Elite Virtual GP and at-home care via eMed x Livi Workplace pension through Penfold, with salary sacrifice option Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay with additional time available at reduced pay Referral Instructions If you are being referred for the role, please contact that person to apply on your behalf. Other notices Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records. Beware of recruiting scams: Ramp will only contact you through official @ Ramp.com email addresses and will never ask for payment or sensitive personal information during the hiring process. Ramp Applicant Privacy Notice",
