    "summaryAr": "Who We Are Notion is the collaborative AI workspace where teams and agents think together . We're building one place where your knowledge, projects, meetings, and AI tools live side by side, so work is faster, clearer, and less fragmented. Millions of individuals, small teams, and large companies run their work on Notion. Notinos (our employees) are customer zero in bringing this future of work to life. We care about",
    "descriptionAr": "Who We Are Notion is the collaborative AI workspace where teams and agents think together . We're building one place where your knowledge, projects, meetings, and AI tools live side by side, so work is faster, clearer, and less fragmented. Millions of individuals, small teams, and large companies run their work on Notion. Notinos (our employees) are customer zero in bringing this future of work to life. We care about craft, building things that last, and the belief that great work is still fundamentally human. Our goal isn’t to ship the next feature. Each and every team of Notinos is working to set the standard for how humans work together in the AI era. From building a business’s system of record to making and managing AI agents to automating away the busy work, we care deeply about giving our customers more time for their life’s work. About the Role: Notion is reimagining how enterprise software is sold and the Solutions Consultant is the cornerstone of that model. As an SC for the Enterprise market for France, you’ll own the full customer journey: from prospecting, first meeting through workflow design, commercial close, workflow implementation, expansion & renewal planning. You are the single owner of your accounts, accountable for ensuring what you sell actually gets realized. You’ll build live in front of customers, translate workflow designs into commercial outcomes, and be a trusted partner with genuine continuity across the entire relationship. If you’re a builder who loves to sell—and you want to work at the intersection of AI, productivity, and enterprise—this is the role. This role will be based in Paris. We work from our offices on Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays (our Anchor Days) because we do our best thinking and building together in person. We’re looking for someone who’s excited to work alongside the team during those days. About Notion in France While our local team is still growing, France is already Notion’s largest market in EMEA by number of users. Teams at more than 80% of CAC 40 companies use Notion, and we’re proud to support French organisations including Qonto, Pennylane, Alan and AXA Climate. As we grow our presence in France, you’ll have the opportunity to build on that momentum and help shape what comes next. ⁠⁠ ⁠⁠ ⁠⁠ ⁠⁠ What You'll Achieve: Own the full customer lifecycle—new logo, expansion, and renewal—as the single account owner for your book of business, with responsibility for ensuring credits sold translate into credits consumed Build and own a strong pipeline of self-sourced opportunities across your target accounts through proactive outbound prospecting. Design and build workflow solutions live with customers: the discovery is the demo, not the slide deck—you’ll run discovery, design current-to-future-state workflow architecture, and co-build in Notion with the customer Partner with BDRs on target account planning and co-own the outbound motion for your book, running direct outreach to priority stakeholders alongside BDR-sourced pipeline Navigate commercial sizing, proposal construction, procurement, legal, and security review to close deals with the right scope, credits, and implementation path Guide customers through early implementation with a clear adoption plan and handoff to Outcomes Architects for ongoing multi-workflow expansion Partner with Outcomes Architects (OA) on onboarding, adoption plans, expansion strategies, and renewal execution—owning the commercial arc while OAs drive day-to-day workflow adoption Skills You'll Need to Bring: Experience selling technical products to technical buyers in the enterprise segment (3000+ employees) Be a self-starter who owns your pipeline —proactively generating opportunities through prospecting and outbound outreach, and driving them from first contact through to conversion. Technical fluency and genuine comfort building live in software—you can demo, co-design, and troubleshoot in front of a customer without a specialist in the room Strong prospecting, discovery and qualification instincts, with the ability to map customer workflows and translate them into commercial outcomes and adoption plans Experience running complex, multi-stakeholder interactions including procurement, legal, and security review cycles Strong You can own the room - you operate with agency and urgency to bring new ideas and workflows to our customers and present simple ways to solve complex problems A self-starter who owns your pipeline—proactively generating opportunities through prospecting and outbound outreach, and driving them from first contact through to conversion You’re obsessed with AI, constantly building with the newest tools & learning new ways of working Native or bilingual level fluency French business-level English proficiency. Nice to Haves: Full-cycle B2B software sales experience or solutions engineering experience with a consistent track record of exceeding quota across new logo acquisition and expansion motions Familiarity with usage-based or consumption-based pricing models and the ability to structure credit-based commercial proposals Prior experience selling to mid-market and enterprise accounts in productivity, collaboration, or workflow software Experience in a shared account ownership model, partnering with a post-sale or CS team as part of an integrated customer motion Notion is committed to providing highly competitive cash compensation, equity, and benefits. The compensation offered for this role will be based on multiple factors such as location, the role's scope and complexity, and the candidate's experience and expertise, and may vary from the range provided below. The estimated range for total on target earnings (including base salary and on target incentive pay) for this role is €270,000 per year. By clicking “Submit Application”, I understand and agree that Notion and its affiliates and subsidiaries will collect and process my information in accordance with Notion’s Global Recruiting Privacy ",
